WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.400
A variable holds one thing. But what if your game needs to remember ten names, or fifty high scores? You need a list!

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.713
A list is like a variable with numbered boxes.

3
00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:23.600
Item 1, item 2, item 3… One list can hold many words or numbers.

4
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.348
Use “item (2) of fruits” to read the second thing.

5
00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:35.365
The length of the list tells you how many items it holds.

6
00:00:35.965 --> 00:00:40.243
Lists remember items even after the program stops.

7
00:00:40.243 --> 00:00:47.565
Use “delete all of” when the flag is clicked so the list doesn’t keep growing.

8
00:00:48.165 --> 00:00:54.183
Pick a random position from 1 to the length of the list.

9
00:00:54.183 --> 00:00:59.765
This is how games choose a random word, question or prize.

10
00:01:00.365 --> 00:01:04.209
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

11
00:01:04.209 --> 00:01:09.357
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
